60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The candidates are here. I see Night Service Extension, Crosstown Bus Corridor, Station Access Upgrades, and Integrated Fare Platform. Which one survives our constraints?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Asuka, the audits show waiting kills the trip, not ticketing. The Crosstown Corridor fixes the mid-city delay.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Takumi, the corridor needs paving rates we cannot afford. The ledger is bleeding, and the technology line is already trimmed.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Benjamin, the ledger is tight, but the accessibility records show four rebuilds finished on time. The ground is known, unlike the shells.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the records are clean, but the shells are not. I cannot vote for anything that risks unrecorded voids stopping the work for weeks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Benjamin, the fare platform is a software fix, not a staffing one. It doesn't require the bodies we lack.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Asuka, the audits prove waiting is the killer, not ticketing. The fare platform ignores the mid-city delay entirely.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the fare platform is cheap, but the contractor fees are already eating our paving budget. We cannot afford another hidden cost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"-Servas: @Benjamin, the fees are a symptom, not the cause. The accessibility records show what actually sticks. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the records are clean, but the shells are not. I cannot vote for anything that risks unrecorded voids stopping the work for weeks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the records are clean, but the rosters are not. I cannot vote for upgrades that require crews we do not have.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the audits show waiting is the killer, not ticketing. The fare platform ignores the mid-city delay entirely.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the corridor is a money pit. The fare platform is the only option that doesn't require new crews or paving.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the fare platform is a trap. The minutes show the partners never agreed on data terms. I cannot build on a broken foundation.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the fare platform is a trap. The minutes show the partners never agreed on data terms. I cannot build on a broken foundation.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the fare platform is a trap. The minutes show the partners never agreed on data terms. I cannot build on a broken foundation.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Benjamin, the fare platform is a trap. The minutes show the partners never agreed on data terms. I cannot build on a broken foundation.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concede the data point. The fare platform is dead. I vote for the Crosstown Corridor; it is the only option that doesn't require new crews.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the corridor is a trap. The paving rates are climbing, and the ledger is bleeding. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I vote for Station Access Upgrades. The records show it works, and the maintenance contract has spare capacity. The shells are too risky.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
